    "html": "<h2>Batch 86 Forensic Discoveries</h2>\n<p>Batch 86 recovers and dates 13 historical broadcasts spanning aviation war drama, Hollywood gossip columnists, pioneering country-pop auditions, romantic crooner variety, home-front wartime cooking, and overseas military soundtrack exclusives: 2 December 1942 dramatic broadcasts written, directed, and narrated by Orson Welles for Lockheed-Vega aircraft builders on <em><strong>Ceiling Unlimited</strong></em>, 3 spring 1940 Hollywood dispatches featuring gossip queen Hedda Hopper and rising RKO comedic talent Lucille Ball on <em><strong>Tonight in Hollywood</strong></em>, a rare 1949 Lang-Worth transcription audition co-starring bandleader Ray Anthony and young vocalist Patti Page on <em><strong>The Rhythm Rendezvous</strong></em>, Latin-pop crooner Andy Russell hosting lyricist Johnny Mercer on <em><strong>The Andy Russell Show</strong></em> (1946), guitar virtuoso Arthur Smith picking &#39;Peter Cottontail&#39; on <em><strong>Arthur Smith&#39;s Corner Store</strong></em> (WBT Charlotte, 1950), wartime rationing recipes from John MacPherson on <em><strong>The Mystery Chef</strong></em> (1943), transatlantic aviator Harry Richman with jazz stylist Lee Wiley (1937), Elvis Presley&#39;s <em>Speedway</em> soundtrack on AFRS, and network comedy previews on <em><strong>The Adventures of Ozzie and Harriet</strong></em>.</p>\n<hr>\n<h2>1. <em>Ceiling Unlimited</em> &amp; <em>Tonight in Hollywood</em> (1940–1942)</h2>\n<p>Wartime aerospace drama and classic Hollywood talk:</p>\n<table>\n<thead>\n<tr>\n<th>Original Circulating Filename</th>\n<th>Canonical Title</th>\n<th>Verified Airdate</th>\n<th>Broadcast Substance</th>\n</tr>\n</thead>\n<tbody><tr>\n<td><code>Ceiling_Unlimited_Time_Space.mp3</code></td>\n<td><strong>&quot;Ceiling Unlimited: Orson Welles on &#39;Voyages by Man in Time and Space&#39;&quot;</strong></td>\n<td><strong>1942-12-14</strong></td>\n<td>Welles dramatizing aviation history, aerodynamics, and global transport.</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code>Ceiling_Unlimited_Sabotage.mp3</code></td>\n<td><strong>&quot;Ceiling Unlimited: Orson Welles on &#39;Wartime Aviation &amp; Industrial Sabotage&#39;&quot;</strong></td>\n<td><strong>1942-12-21</strong></td>\n<td>Tense home-front aircraft factory drama highlighting counter-espionage.</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code>Tonight_Hollywood_Lucy_1.mp3</code></td>\n<td><strong>&quot;Tonight in Hollywood: Hedda Hopper interviews Lucille Ball (Broadcast 1)&quot;</strong></td>\n<td><strong>1940-03-22</strong></td>\n<td>Hedda Hopper and Lucille Ball discussing comedy acting and RKO projects.</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code>Tonight_Hollywood_Gossip.mp3</code></td>\n<td><strong>&quot;Tonight in Hollywood: Hedda Hopper Hollywood Gossip &amp; Movie Previews&quot;</strong></td>\n<td><strong>1940-03-29</strong></td>\n<td>Studio scoops, fashion notes, and behind-the-scenes film gossip.</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code>Tonight_Hollywood_Lucy_2.mp3</code></td>\n<td><strong>&quot;Tonight in Hollywood: Hedda Hopper interviews Lucille Ball (Broadcast 2)&quot;</strong></td>\n<td><strong>1940-04-05</strong></td>\n<td>Lucy joking about studio schedules and dance rehearsals.</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody></table>\n<hr>\n<h2>2. <em>Rhythm Rendezvous</em>, <em>Andy Russell</em>, &amp; <em>Arthur Smith</em></h2>\n<table>\n<thead>\n<tr>\n<th>Original Circulating Filename</th>\n<th>Canonical Title</th>\n<th>Verified Airdate</th>\n<th>Performers &amp; Repertoire</th>\n</tr>\n</thead>\n<tbody><tr>\n<td><code>Rhythm_Rendezvous_Page_Anthony.mp3</code></td>\n<td><strong>&quot;The Rhythm Rendezvous: Ray Anthony Orchestra &amp; Patti Page Audition&quot;</strong></td>\n<td><strong>1949-05-18</strong></td>\n<td>Pre-fame Patti Page demonstrating her warm, pitch-perfect vocals.</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code>Andy_Russell_Johnny_Mercer.mp3</code></td>\n<td><strong>&quot;The Andy Russell Show: &#39;Magic Is the Moonlight&#39; (Guest Johnny Mercer)&quot;</strong></td>\n<td><strong>1946-06-09</strong></td>\n<td>Andy Russell serenading listeners and joking with Capitol Records co-founder Johnny Mercer.</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code>Arthur_Smith_Peter_Cottontail.mp3</code></td>\n<td><strong>&quot;Arthur Smith&#39;s Corner Store: &#39;Peter Cottontail &amp; Down Home Pickin&#39;&#39;&quot;</strong></td>\n<td><strong>1950-04-04</strong></td>\n<td>Arthur &#39;Guitar Boogie&#39; Smith and his Crackerjacks in Charlotte.</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code>Mystery_Chef_Butter_Recipe.mp3</code></td>\n<td><strong>&quot;The Mystery Chef: &#39;Wartime Butter Stretching &amp; Household Economy&#39;&quot;</strong></td>\n<td><strong>1943-05-18</strong></td>\n<td>Practical kitchen advice under wartime point rationing.</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code>Harry_Richman_Lee_Wiley.mp3</code></td>\n<td><strong>&quot;Harry Richman - It&#39;s Florida&#39;s Treat: &#39;Keep Your Sunny Side Up&#39; (Guest Lee Wiley)&quot;</strong></td>\n<td><strong>1937-02-17</strong></td>\n<td>State of Florida musical variety with legendary jazz vocalist Lee Wiley.</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code>AFRS_Elvis_Speedway_1.mp3</code></td>\n<td><strong>&quot;AFRS Presents: &#39;Speedway Soundtrack Special - Elvis Presley&#39; (Part 1)&quot;</strong></td>\n<td><strong>1968-06-25</strong></td>\n<td>Armed Forces Radio Service broadcast of Elvis&#39;s MGM soundtrack.</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code>AFRS_Elvis_Speedway_2.mp3</code></td>\n<td><strong>&quot;AFRS Presents: &#39;Speedway Soundtrack Special - Elvis Presley&#39; (Part 2)&quot;</strong></td>\n<td><strong>1968-07-02</strong></td>\n<td>Nancy Sinatra duet &#39;Your Groovy Self&#39; and rock tracks for overseas troops.</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code>Ozzie_Harriet_Promo.mp3</code></td>\n<td><strong>&quot;The Adventures of Ozzie and Harriet: Special Network Preview &amp; Comedy Promo&quot;</strong></td>\n<td><strong>1949-09-23</strong></td>\n<td>Ozzie and Harriet Nelson introducing the upcoming fall radio season.</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody></table>\n",
